(text "IF STAGE" (rect -8 616 189 669)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "IF/ID Pipeline Register" (rect 936 -80 1413 -27)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "Note that the imem already has a register at its output q_a, " (rect 960 424 1463 447)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "therefore, there is no need to buffer the instruction in the " (rect 960 440 1452 463)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "IF/ID pipeline register. In other words, consider q_a port as " (rect 960 456 1461 479)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "a part of the output port of the IF/ID pipeline register." (rect 960 472 1415 495)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "Note: the instruction memory here is 8KW or 32KB." (rect 640 520 1074 543)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "We just need pc bits 14~2 to address the 8K instruction words" (rect 576 536 1110 559)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "ID STAGE" (rect 1592 760 1796 813)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "ID/EX Pipeline Register" (rect 2184 -80 2680 -27)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "EX STAGE" (rect 2888 808 3103 861)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "EX/MEM Pipeline Register" (rect 3392 -88 3947 -35)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "register file" (rect 1568 232 1760 275)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "main control" (rect 1536 0 1754 43)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "immediate generator" (rect 1552 616 1909 659)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "branch comparator" (rect 1864 232 2194 275)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "PC register" (rect 352 464 538 507)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "ALU" (rect 3160 40 3231 83)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "ALU control unit" (rect 2944 560 3224 603)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "MEM STAGE" (rect 4032 752 4295 805)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "MEM/WB Pipeline Register" (rect 4448 -96 5020 -43)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "Note that the imem and dmem have their own registers to buffer their read data, " (rect 4416 -32 5106 -9)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "these registers are considered as a part of the MEM/WB pipeline register." (rect 4416 -16 5036 7)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "The address checker here guarantees that the" (rect 3864 424 4255 447)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "WB STAGE" (rect 5032 712 5264 765)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "Final Pipeline Register" (rect 5496 -104 5973 -51)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "This extra pipeline register is to buffer the result of register-writing instructions. " (rect 5456 -32 6138 -9)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "The assembler textbook mentions that if the WB stage of a producer and the ID stage" (rect 5456 8 6180 31)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "of a consumer overlap in the same cycle, the producer uses the first half of the cycle to" (rect 5456 32 6188 55)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "write to the destination register, and the consumer uses the second half to read from it." (rect 5456 56 6195 79)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "As introducing a 2X faster clock into the schemeatics will compicate the design, we added " (rect 5456 104 6223 127)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "this extra pipeline register to extend the time of the producer in the pipeline for 1 more cycle" (rect 5456 128 6252 151)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "As a result, we can forward from this register to the consumer just like from the previous" (rect 5456 160 6201 183)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "two pipeline registers." (rect 5456 184 5644 207)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "Components and ports for simulation purposes" (rect 4920 -296 5728 -253)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "instruction memory" (rect 704 312 1039 355)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "Global Clock and Reset Signals" (rect 288 -96 948 -43)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 20)))
(text "This part of the circuit is not in your textbook. It is used to avoid letting any instruction enter the pipeline" (rect 232 872 1119 895)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "during the reset of the CPU" (rect 232 888 464 911)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "address issued by CPU to write the data memory is in 0x00008000 - 0x0000FFFF " (rect 3864 448 4569 471)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 8)))
(text "Data Memory" (rect 4056 224 4284 267)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
(text "single adder to generate PC + 4" (rect 184 40 719 83)(font "Intel Clear" (font_size 16)))
